    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="0803" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13231: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-14T19:00:00-05:00">October 14, 1935—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Your 53, October 12, 2 p.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d691-f1"/> The Department
                    refers to the warning given by Hankow to American citizens at Lanchow and
                    suggests that the Embassy, if in its opinion the situation warrants, may care to
                    reenforce Hankow’s warning by communicating through the American Consul General
                    at Shanghai with the headquarters there of the American missions concerned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
